{#-
  Bootcamp_Power manifest — powers/senzing-bootcamp/plugin.json.

  Rendered by the `manifest` rule (kind: generate) in contract.yaml. Produces the
  Agent Plugins v1.0.0 plugin document: the fixed top-level field set, plus all
  Senzing/Kiro provenance under `extensions["com.senzing.bootcamp"]` because the
  schema's top-level field set is closed (R2 AC5, design defect D3).

  Render context — every name below is REQUIRED. Render with
  `jinja2.StrictUndefined` so a missing value raises rather than emitting an empty
  field; a silently empty `version` would defeat the version-match check (R2 AC3).

    tag                  str  ResolvedRelease.tag — the resolved Template_Release
                              tag, e.g. "0.5.1". Written to `version` and to
                              `extensions[...].templateRelease` character-for-character
                              (R2 AC1, AC2, AC5).
    template_repository  str  ResolvedRelease.repository — the Template_Plugin
                              "owner/name" slug, e.g. "Senzing/senzing-bootcamp-claude-plugin".
    contract_version     int  contract.yaml `contractVersion` — the transformation
                              contract that produced this Power (R3).

  Determinism (R16 AC8, Property 4): keys are literal and in fixed order, values come
  only from the context above, and nothing here reads a clock, a run id, an environment
  variable, or the filesystem — so the same (contract, source, tag) renders byte-identical
  output. Render with `keep_trailing_newline=True` and write with `newline="\n"` so the
  file ends in exactly one LF.

  `license` is fixed at "Apache-2.0" to match the repository root LICENSE (R4 AC4, R14 AC3).
  Identity fields (name, description, author, homepage, repository, keywords) are Kiro-owned
  constants, not template-derived, so they are literal here rather than context-supplied.
-#}
{%- set template_repository_url = "https://github.com/" ~ template_repository -%}
{
  "$schema": "https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/plugin.schema.json",
  "name": "senzing-bootcamp",
  "version": {{ tag | tojson }},
  "description": "Guided Senzing entity resolution bootcamp. Use when learning Senzing, working through the bootcamp modules, or onboarding to entity resolution.",
  "author": { "name": "Senzing", "url": "https://senzing.com" },
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "homepage": {{ template_repository_url | tojson }},
  "repository": "https://github.com/docktermj/senzing-bootcamp-kiro-powers-development",
  "keywords": ["senzing", "entity-resolution", "bootcamp", "training", "onboarding", "data-quality"],
  "extensions": {
    "com.senzing.bootcamp": {
      "templateRepository": {{ template_repository_url | tojson }},
      "templateRelease": {{ tag | tojson }},
      "contractVersion": {{ contract_version | int }}
    }
  }
}
